# CONFLATION 1 -- `arg` differs STRUCTURALLY but `repr(arg)` is IDENTICAL.
#   MEASURED: repr(arg) before=None after=None equal=True  and the normal form's arg text before='N' after='N'
#   So a differ keying on `repr` would report NO difference here, and a differ keying on structure must report the `src` field.
#   ALLOC 2/2  CONST 4/4  MUL 1/1  PERMUTE 2/2  REDUCE 1/1  RESHAPE 4/4  STACK 4/4
# SHARED cores=15  ONLY-ORDERED=0  ONLY-SRCSWAP=0  field-mismatches=0  rung2-pairs=3  rung3.5-crossrefs=0  zip-truncated=0
# RUNG 2 -- paired on the dtype- and depth-erased arg, so these ARE the same node:
MISMATCH PERMUTE   py#17 vs srcswap#17  (no shared core; paired one-to-one on the dtype- and depth-erased arg)
    src  py=['07a90938'] bend=['d1670d45']
MISMATCH MUL       py#16 vs srcswap#16  (no shared core; paired one-to-one on the dtype- and depth-erased arg)
    src  py=['2b7d1a7e', 'bd57da94'] bend=['bd57da94', '2b7d1a7e']
MISMATCH REDUCE    py#18 vs srcswap#18  (no shared core; paired one-to-one on the dtype- and depth-erased arg)
    src  py=['06ff9493'] bend=['76377eb2']
#   z   arg         py=0    bend=0    a realized BUFFER: device-object PRESENCE only
#       Buffer has no `slot` (measured) and the port's is a P6 allocator slot; size/dtype/device/offset are already ParamArg fields 2/3/8 and ARE compared
#   y   arg         py=0    bend=0    a bytes arg: CONTENT compared; the residual is the bytes CONST
#       MEASURED 2026-10-04: `ABlob{bs}` (ops.bend:1062) holds the BYTES and `eq_arg.ABlob` (:1801) compares them, so the column is the full byte list; this row used to say LENGTH only. NOT comparable: a bytes CONST -- upstream's `PyConst` includes `bytes` (ops.py:122), the port's `Const` is CBool|CInt|CFloat|CInvalid (ops.bend:808-811), and graphcmp.bend's `konst` has no bytes arm at all
#   u   arg         py=0    bend=0    a UOp nested in an arg: identity NOT compared
#       measured: PYLITERAL's nested UOp is in neither `src` nor `toposort`, so it has no arena index here; the port's ATuple also spells PERMUTE's literal ints
#   B   arg         py=0    bend=0    a bool ATOM in a FLIP arg, CANONICALISED to the u32 atom: CONTENT compared
#       FLIPR-1 (`canon_flip`). This row is the ONLY thing that changed about the `flip` verdict's arg, and it is a count of SUBSTITUTIONS, not of omissions: upstream types FLIP's arg `tuple[bool,...]` (movement.py:253) and the port types it `List<&2,U32>` (ops.bend:1066), while MEASURED `UOp(FLIP,src,(True,False)) is UOp(FLIP,src,(1,0))` -> True in BOTH request orders and for PERMUTE too, because the ucache hashes VALUES and `True == 1`. So one node, two spellings, and `ops.py:428`'s bool guard is INSERTION-ORDER DEPENDENT. The py side is the only one that can produce a `B` here; a py=0/bend=0 run is a corpus fact, not a claim that no FLIP exists
#   q   arg         py=0    bend=0    an applied option the port cannot resolve: COUNT only
#       ops.bend:978 types applied_opts/opts_to_apply as List<U32>; upstream's elements are `Opt` dataclasses and no port file writes a non-empty list
#   X!  arg         py=0    bend=0    an AxisType member with no counterpart at this tree
#       measured at 3138973dc: `list(AxisType)` is DEVICE..PLACEHOLDER (8). The port keeps AXIS_REDUCE and AXIS_UNROLL, DELETED upstream by 78d482262, for six committed files
#   BAD arg         py=0    bend=0    the port's arena bottom: not a node
#       ops.bend:1154 -- a read of an index that was never interned
#   ?   dtype/shape py=0    bend=0    the port's fold produced no Derived for this node, in BOTH columns
#       PORT-ONLY, no upstream counterpart: `UOp.shape` always raises or returns a tuple (ops.py:455) and `dtype_from_uop` (ops.py:123-190) is TOTAL over Ops, so upstream has no third state in either column and `?` cannot be produced by the py side. FIRST LIVE on `--graph sym`: fold.bend's `marg.of` answered None for a STACK element that is not a CONST (the `ssimplify` wall), which unsettled the RESHAPE's whole `Derived` and so took `dtype` with it. NO LONGER LIVE THERE -- `sym_dim` and `reshape_ok` closed it and `sym` reads `?=0`; the row is kept and asserted on `--graph loop`, whose CALL has a different and still-open cause (`call_dt` reads `CallInfo.dtype`, which CPython's `CallInfo` does not have). **It was TWO port defects, not one**: the revert of either half puts `sym` back to `?=0/6` and DISAGREE (measured, `runs/margsym/M16-sym-DISAGREE.txt`)
#   E   arg         py=0    bend=0    an enum member outside {Ops, AxisType, AddrSpace}: NAME only
#       `OptOps` (codegen/opt/__init__.py:6). Before the enum arm this CRASHED: the generic `vars()` fallback followed `__objclass__` into the enum CLASS, walked its 17 attributes, and died on a descriptor -- so a SINK with a non-empty applied_opts could not be emitted at all
#   -   arg   py=n/a  bend=n/a  KernelInfo.estimates: NEITHER SIDE CARRIES IT (port dropped it, P5); upstream's value is None for every kernel the port can build, so the count would be 0 BY CONSTRUCTION and is not printed as one
